<ol class="steps">
  <li>
    <span class="se"><b>§ 01</b> Edit</span>
    Edit <code>global/AGENTS.md</code>, merge it to <code>master</code>, and pull. <code>gap sync</code> only publishes merged rules.
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="se"><b>§ 02</b> Sync</span>
    Run <code>gap sync</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="se"><b>§ 03</b> Check</span>
    Run <code>gap status</code> to see each component's pin and any skill drift. It writes nothing and exits 1 on drift.
  </li>
</ol>
<div class="codewrap">
  <div class="bar"><span>Terminal</span><button type="button" class="copy-cmd">Copy</button></div>
  <pre class="code"><span class="p">$ </span>gap sync
<span class="p">$ </span>gap status</pre>
</div>
<div class="callout"><b>Note</b><p><code>gap status</code> writes nothing and exits 1 on drift. That is a signal, not a crash.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><b>Note</b><p>Only <code>gap pin &lt;id&gt;@&lt;ref&gt;</code> moves a pin in <code>gap.lock</code>.</p></div>
<div class="callout tip">
  <b>Tip</b>
  <p>
    If sync asks about a file it did not write, answer in a terminal. In an agent's shell with no terminal, it prints
    <code>Refusing to replace foreign file</code>, skips that file, publishes the rest, and exits 1.
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy-cmd');
  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText('gap sync\ngap status');
      button.textContent = 'Copied';
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        button.textContent = 'Copy';
      }, 1200);
    } catch {
      button.textContent = 'Failed';
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        button.textContent = 'Copy';
      }, 1600);
    }
  });
</script>
